From 768506c94f61906a6b9066ca54fcb2cf7973213c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: go-while <go-while@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 14:06:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] tests/overview: Close Xref searches before testing
 cancellation

The test kept every search handle open after checking its article, and
with it a reference to the mapped group data, through the later
cancellation checks.  On OpenBSD those checks then still saw the
cancelled entries; with the handles closed, they pass.

Why the reopened data does not show the cancellation while the old
mappings are alive is not established here, nor whether a search that
a reader holds open has the same effect.  This change only stops the
test from leaking the handles.

Co-Authored-By: GPT-6.1 Sol <noreply@openai.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 tests/overview/xref-t.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tests/overview/xref-t.c b/tests/overview/xref-t.c
index 169792f8c..f6a170920 100644
--- a/tests/overview/xref-t.c
+++ b/tests/overview/xref-t.c
@@ -158,6 +158,10 @@ overview_load(int n, const char *data, struct overview *overview)
                 ok_int(n++, strlen(start) + (result - article.overview) + 2,
                        article.overlen);
             }
+            /* Release the search's reference to the mapped data before the
+               cancellation checks; with it held, they failed on OpenBSD. */
+            if (search != NULL)
+                overview_search_close(overview, search);
         }
     }
     fclose(overdata);
